  "body": "The user wants Sodick wire EDM support, including 4-axis (taper / U V) cuts.\n\nToday the Sodick post refuses 4-axis cuts by name, on purpose (#1497, PR #2120, decision `docs/decisions/1497-sodick-four-axis.md`). In the 1998 Sodick manual, U V are offsets from X Y; X Y sit on the part's bottom plane; and the program planes are measured from the worktable. CamCraft's machine file and toolpath stream state the wire guide planes, but not the worktable heights, so the guide-plane values cannot be converted to Sodick's planes. Writing them unconverted would post a wrong 4-axis cut.\n\nWhat is needed:\n- Machine-file keys for the Sodick plane heights the manual uses (worktable to lower guide, worktable to program plane / part bottom, upper guide), with sources; refusal by name when a taper cut needs them and they are missing.\n- The conversion from CamCraft's guide planes to Sodick's planes, from the published manual only (clean-room).\n- G74/G75 output and U V words, with goldens; an air-cut test kit for an owner of a Sodick (the Discord user who has one).\n\nDone means: a machine file that states the heights posts a 4-axis taper cut whose U V and plane words match the manual's worked example; without the heights, the cut is refused by name; existing 2-axis output is byte-identical.\n\nRefs #1497, #617.\n",
